    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look poised for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66). **Jackson Merrill** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Littell, whose 4.63 xERA offers a prime opportunity for sustained production, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** capitalizes on a dynamic platoon advantage and the run-production potential inherent in the #2 spot. **Kyle Tucker** (70.98) and **Gunnar Henderson** (70.51) remain essential anchors, providing the elite floor we require; **Gunnar Henderson** specifically thrives despite the threat of Miles, as our park factor metrics and his high xwOBA metrics project him to punch through the 2.95 xERA barrier. **Sam Antonacci** remains a critical component of our strategy to steal points in the scarcest category, as his #1 spot in the order and solid 66.09 score make him a vital engine for runs and SBs.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Liam Hicks**, who finished with a 39.58 score, just narrowly missing our 40-point threshold for active play. While his platoon advantage against McLean provided a slight bump, the combination of a tough 3.03 xERA for the opposing starter and the restrictive \"Zebras Floor\" forced our hand to keep him benched to protect our season-long game caps. Conversely, we are navigating the continued absence of **Jordan Westburg**, **Jorge Polanco**, and **Drake Baldwin**, who remain on the IL. We are monitoring **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (56.40) and **Josh Jung** (58.60) closely; while they are comfortably in the lineup, they are facing top-tier arms in Bradish and Wacha, respectively. We trust their current form, but will be watching for any late-inning defensive substitutions if the game script turns stagnant.",
